# std/copy — one of the file tools (std/files holds the source they share).
# The help is a HERE-STRING so it lives in this expression, which is stripped
# from the tree the build sees: editing the docs re-keys this tool's ArgTree and
# nothing it builds from.
HELP=<<END
Copy a file or directory to a new path, creating any missing parent directories. `root` is a directory holding both paths, such as sources/repo for a stack's layers (`.` for the whole session); `from` and `to` are relative to it. The destination must not exist. The copy is the entry itself: a source tree stays a source tree, with its history. Prefer this over cp via bash.
@param from Path to copy, relative to root, such as 00-base.
@param to Path of the copy, relative to root, such as 99-dirty.
@writer
@root
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=DEEP-DEPS/files
curry --base=$IMAGE --op=copy --help=$HELP
